From d726cb510a0d31036e46b3007d968477a2d5cf85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:13:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Keep Inkling 2's cards busy through a prompt with experts in
 RAM

Bartowski's Q4_K_M read a 60K prompt at ~1975 tok/s in the pool
against UD-Q4_K_XL's ~2350, with each card idle 6 s of 30. Now:

- the prompt GEMM's converters (k_expert_ws) take a weight's bytes
  into numbers without conversion instructions (16 a clock an SM):
  a byte into a half's mantissa (1024 + q, Q8_0 / Q5_0: the offset
  off exactly, one rounding by d) or a float's (2^23 + q, the
  K-quants), the 2-byte aligned rows read 16 bits at a time; the
  same values. A visit's launches at 60K: Q5_0 down 3.79 -> 2.55
  ms, Q8_0 down 3.35 -> 2.81, Q4_K gate-up 4.92 -> 4.72, Q5_K 6.3
  -> 5.6, Q6_K 18.6 -> 17.8;
- a staged visit no longer reads the routing back (a host sync a
  visit, so a host thread could not queue past one): a chunk's
  routings reach all of a layer's experts, so every expert in RAM is
  copied, in batches whose order, pointers and sizes are the
  layer's, built again when its experts in VRAM change (k_group
  keeps listed experts' empty groups, so their numbers are known);
- the two-card split takes the fastest of the pipeline estimates to
  1% (5% let through splits whose hand-offs leave a card waiting:
  layers 0-5, 11-16 on card 0 for Bartowski's, 4-7% slower than
  0-5, 12-17);
- decode: native_qrows_kernel reads Q4_K gate-up and Q5_0 / Q8_0
  down rows at Inkling's shapes from 4 rows a step (a verify): 4 / 8
  lanes a row, each a ninth of it, the group's entries' q8_1 rows in
  shared memory, every weight read once for all of them (an 8-row
  step 64.7 -> 54-59 ms; to 3 rows the generic kernels, as fast).

The converters and the staging: output and perplexity bit for bit
the same. The split: a 59K-token perplexity 2.9914 -> 2.9820 (the
rows' rounding); decode's rows within ~1e-7 of the generic kernels.

Two cards, the pool at 512K: Bartowski's prompt 7K 1839 -> 2024
tok/s, 60K 1974 -> 2208; UD-Q4_K_XL 60K 2350 -> 2443.
